"https://t.co/MvNoVxvECp"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/CWRELQMvPH","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2108509543810605218/photo/1","media_key":"3_2108509531810746368","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/CWRELQMvPH"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/CWRELQMvPH","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2108509543810605218/photo/1","media_key":"3_2108509535006826496","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/CWRELQMvPH"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/CWRELQMvPH","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2108509543810605218/photo/1","media_key":"3_2108509537703780353","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/CWRELQMvPH"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/CWRELQMvPH","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2108509543810605218/photo/1","media_key":"3_2108509541138878464","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/CWRELQMvPH"},{"display_url":"x.com/2311987360/sta…","end":324,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/2311987360/status/2106333942911758358","start":301,"url":"https://t.co/KHktzOC3PT"}]},"id":"2108509543810605218","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"newsletter.marclou.com","end":133,"expanded_url":"http://newsletter.marclou.com","start":110,"url":"https://t.co/pypYdNhdlZ"}]},"text":"Bye bye Beehiiv 👋\n\nI vibe-coded my own newsletter platform:\n\n📧 Campaign management w/ editor\n🖥️ Web archives (https://t.co/pypYdNhdlZ)\n🔗 API support\n🫧 List cleanup, deliverability reports\n\nIt took a few prompts with Opus 5.5.\n\nI left Beehiiv because they raised prices for the 3rd time in 2 years.\n- My first yearly bill was $1,000.\n- My future bill would have been $4,000.\n\nNow I'm using AWS SES + MongoDB, and I will pay less than $300/year.\n\nNewsletter platforms charge per subscriber, when in fact the real cost is the number of emails sent. Subscribers will naturally become inactive, so you end up paying more for something that hurts your deliverability (sending to dormant subscribers = spam trap).\n\nSo I've set a cleanup cron job for my newsletter alternative. It marks inactive subs as dormant, sends one last re-engaging email, and stops emailing them. Money saved. Deliverability increased.\n\nI also gain a priceless feature: Freedom. I can change the UI, add features, connect all my apps - anything is possible with just a prompt.\n\nI'm replacing Resend next. I love it, but it's very expensive ($400/mo)"},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":497,"impression_count":74855,"like_count":695,"quote_count":38,"reply_count":174,"repost_count":16},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2106333942911758358","type":"quoted"}],"text":"Bye bye Beehiiv 👋\n\nI vibe-coded my own newsletter platform:\n\n📧 Campaign management w/ editor\n🖥️ Web archives (https://t.co/MvNoVxvECp)\n🔗 API support\n🫧 List cleanup, deliverability reports\n\nIt took a few prompts with Opus 5.5.\n\nI left Beehiiv because they raised prices for the https://t.co/CWRELQMvPH https://t.co/KHktzOC3PT","url":"https://x.com/marclou/status/2108509543810605218"},{"author_id":"1573399256836309009","conversation_id":"2108466251882275144","created_at":"2026-10-09T07:55:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2108466251882275144"],"id":"2108466251882275144","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"It's an irony of history that OpenAI and Anthropic have essentially swapped places again. All the criticisms leveled at Anthropic just a few months ago (inefficiency, poor rates, poor communication, etc.) have now completely turned against OpenAI, and Anthropic has taken over OpenAI's position as position as the good and friendly frontier lab."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":66,"impression_count":50636,"like_count":1419,"quote_count":9,"reply_count":118,"repost_count":38},"text":"It's an irony of history that OpenAI and Anthropic have essentially swapped places again. All the criticisms leveled at Anthropic just a few months ago (inefficiency, poor rates, poor communication, etc.) have now completely turned against OpenAI, a